\yii\\db\\ActiveQuery\r\n\t */\r\n\tpublic function getClientbis()\r\n\t{\r\n\t\treturn Annuaire::find()\r\n\t\t\t->join('JOIN', 'annuaire_dossier', 'annuaire_dossier.id_annuaire=annuaire.id')\r\n\t\t\t->where(['actif'=>1, 'annuaire_dossier.type'=>'client', 'annuaire_dossier.id_dossier'=>$this->id]);\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n```\r\nUse this method via the getter magic method\r\n\r\n```php\r\necho $dossier->clientbis->nom;\r\n```\r\n\r\n### What is the expected result?\r\nReturn a result of the ActiveQuery\r\n\r\n### What do you get instead?\r\nAn error Invalid argument supplied for foreach()\r\nin yii\\vendor\\yiisoft\\yii2\\db\\BaseActiveRecord.php line 1732\r\n\r\n### Additional info\r\nReturn a ActiveQuery without a proper hasOne() or hasMany() seem a bad practice for me, but i am not sure of that.\r\nStill, it work well in Yii < 2.0.14.\r\nSince this is a minor update, maybe a fix could ease the upgrade process, or a new Exception could explain the problem ?\r\n\r\n| Q                | A\r\n| ---------------- | ---\r\n| Yii version      | 2.0.14\r\n| PHP version      | 5.6.31\r\n| Operating system | Windows 10\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"SilverFire","id":4499203,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTkyMDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4499203?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverFire","html_url":"https://github.com/SilverFire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverFire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverFire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverFire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverFire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverFire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverFire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverFire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverFire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com